1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,200
Shared machines are used by everyone and looked after by no one. COMMONKIT gives each one its own NEAR account.

2
00:00:03,200 --> 00:00:05,067
Open the app. No wallet is needed to look around.

3
00:00:05,067 --> 00:00:07,767
The app: Two communities, four shared machines. Everything here is read live from NEAR testnet.

4
00:00:07,767 --> 00:00:09,233
Open the makerlab's 3D printer.

5
00:00:09,233 --> 00:00:13,033
The machine: The printer has its own account with no keys: nobody can empty it. The printer itself is simulated.

6
00:00:13,033 --> 00:00:14,400
To use it, book it.

7
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:20,067
Book: Pick a time. You pay a small fee plus a deposit that comes back after a clean return.

8
00:00:20,067 --> 00:00:23,067
You sign this with a NEAR wallet, and the booking becomes a testnet transaction.

9
00:00:23,067 --> 00:00:29,233
Here is Alex's booking on testnet: reservation_confirmed.

10
00:00:29,233 --> 00:00:33,833
Upkeep: At the printer, a small bridge unlocks it only for a valid booking and reports usage on chain (simulated).

11
00:00:33,833 --> 00:00:39,300
When usage passes a rule, the printer's agent opens an upkeep task. Demo rule: 30 min (real: 200 h).

12
00:00:39,300 --> 00:00:43,700
The task: The task says why it was opened: 4.3 h of nozzle time, over the rule.

13
00:00:43,700 --> 00:00:48,500
Ava did the work, the bridge ran a test print, and Mark, another member, approved it.

14
00:00:48,500 --> 00:00:53,000
Earn: Ava earned two usage rights for this printer. They cannot be sold or moved.

15
00:00:53,000 --> 00:00:58,767
A council member tried to move one of Ava's cards. Refused on chain: E_NON_TRANSFERABLE.

16
00:00:58,767 --> 00:01:03,367
Money: Fees go into the printer's own account, kept under a 3 NEAR cap.

17
00:01:03,367 --> 00:01:08,933
Everything above the cap goes to the community's DAO treasury.

18
00:01:08,933 --> 00:01:13,033
Check it: Every claim can be checked: the Proof page re-reads them from testnet.

19
00:01:13,033 --> 00:01:16,033
Or run ./scripts/verify.sh. No wallet, no keys.
